      en: "The De Molen flour mill is an indispensable component of the national food supply in Suriname. As a central point for processing imported wheat, it provides the essential flour for countless bakeries across the country. This mill is a symbol of industrial self-sufficiency in the staple food sector, ensuring that the population is supplied with high-quality baked goods on a daily basis. Through its central location and efficient logistical integration into the urban supply network, De Molen is a stabilizing factor for food prices and food security."
